course: dictionary
lesson: 5514
title: Leafy and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. Leafy means having lots of leaves, so «a leafy tree» is a tree with many leaves on it.
explain: Leafy can also describe a place. «A leafy street» is a green, pleasant street with many trees and gardens. The clue is the word street: a street cannot have leaves on it, so the word means green and full of trees.
explain: Leafy can describe food too. «Leafy greens» are vegetables that we eat as leaves, such as spinach, lettuce, kale and cabbage. Ask yourself what the word is describing, and the meaning will be clearer.
fact: Leafy is an adjective, so it describes a noun: leafy, leafier, leafiest.
fact: «Leafy» means having lots of leaves, as in «a leafy tree».
fact: «Leafy» can describe a place with many trees and gardens, green and pleasant, as in «a leafy street».
fact: «Leafy greens» are vegetables eaten as leaves, and they are full of vitamins.
fact: Leafy plants need light to make their food, which is called photosynthesis.
exercise: «She sat under the leafy tree and read her book.» What does leafy mean here? | *Having lots of leaves | Very tall and thin | Made of metal | Covered in snow
exercise: «We walked down a leafy street full of gardens.» What does leafy describe? | *A green, pleasant place with many trees | A street made of stone | A street with no cars at all | A very loud, busy road
exercise: Which of these is a leafy green? | Chocolate | Bread | *Lettuce | Rice
test: «The leopard hid on a leafy branch, where sunshine came through the leaves.» Where was the leopard hiding? | On a bare rock | In a deep cave | *On a branch full of leaves | In the sea
test: Which place would most likely be called leafy? | *A quiet street with many trees and gardens | A busy road with no trees | An empty desert | A factory yard
exam: Tom says the sloth is slow because «its leafy food gives little energy». What does leafy mean in this sentence? | Food from the sea | Food that is very sweet | Food that is hot | *Food made from leaves
